From 8f302dabdbd0707f2ad52de1c81a91f626f0ad72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:23:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Air battle sound, release 2: the review's findings mended

An independent review of both air sound patches (21 November) found these;
each was upheld by two readers or checked here.

Voices:
- AudioMaxChannels only lowers the count: the audio quality level's 32 still
  held. DefaultEngine.ini now sets the one quality level to 128 as well, and
  the scene logs how many voices the engine has when it opens.
- Voice priorities were set after the sound had begun, so they did nothing.
  Every take is now made, given its priority, then begun (AAirBattle::Lay).

Guns:
- A fighter's fixed guns of one kind are one take at the square root of how
  many fire (one take per barrel on the same frame added +12 to +18 dB in
  step, into the limiter). The take stops with the wing's last barrel.
- Rounds passing crack by the firing aircraft, not each barrel, the same take
  never again inside air.sameTakeGap, and past the guns' convergence out to
  air.roundsPassing.reach.
- The tally separates takes out of earshot from takes that could not play.

Levels:
- The battle's level eases by the clock (about 1 s), not per frame.
- Formation engine loops use the mix's air.loopsFamily (14 km), and a
  formation that begins out of earshot is begun when it comes nearer.
- Dead engines are counted on the flight core's own engine count per shape.
- A flak burst close to the eye is always heard.
- The master limiter's knee is hard.

The battle's music:
- Zero Hour resolves into The Advance, whatever turn the pieces stood at.
- The theme never comes back at the opening screen's level under a battle
  scene; it comes up when the scene closes.
- Level changes no longer cut a piece's fade-in short (contact's crossfade).
- Without the score's battle pieces the music goes on as it was.
- A battle begun during the last one's stinger gets its score.
- A stinger begun again by the music switch is heard out.

mix.json notes the new air.roundsPassing.reach (1000 m) and the wing rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
